  "slug": "doubling-genome-bb89",
  "summary": "New methods now resolve somatic mutations, mobile element insertions and unmethylated regions in bulk and population-scale sequencing.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is sequencing-based detection of genomic variation that is structured by tissue, epigenetic state or chromatin context. UMR-seq captures unmethylated regions and sequences genetic variants in a single assay, enabling population-scale epigenetic and genetic analysis across diverse plant species. vafSOMA uses tissue composition to detect cell-layer-fixed somatic mutations in plant bulk sequencing and to assign them to layers. In human tissues, a multi-platform framework maps somatic mobile element insertions, benchmarking long-read and MEI-targeted sequencing together with phasing. Separately, explainable machine learning applied to 60 maize and 45 B. rapa genomic and epigenomic features identifies recombination rate and chromatin context as predictors of subgenome identity. The newer element is the pairing of variant detection with tissue structure and chromatin context, applied across plant and human systems.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-09"
}
